      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> February 2026</p>

      <p>This site is run by Chris McCann. Here is what happens with your information when you visit chrismccann.co.</p>

      <p><strong>What I collect</strong></p>

      <p>If you subscribe to Field Notes or take the Field Assessment, I collect your email address. That email goes to Beehiiv, which handles the newsletter. I use it to send you what I said I would send you. Nothing else.</p>

      <p>If you take the Field Assessment, your results (score band, dimension scores) are attached to your subscription so I can send a relevant follow-up. No answers to individual questions are stored.</p>

      <p><strong>Analytics</strong></p>

      <p>This site uses Plausible Analytics, which is privacy-focused and does not use cookies. No personal data is collected. No tracking across sites. Plausible collects aggregate data only: page views, referral sources, country, device type. None of it is tied to an individual.</p>

      <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>

      <p>This site does not set cookies.</p>

      <p><strong>Third parties</strong></p>

      <p>Beehiiv (newsletter delivery), Netlify (hosting), Plausible (analytics), Google Fonts (typography). Each has its own privacy policy. I chose them because they are straightforward about what they do with data.</p>

      <p><strong>Your data</strong></p>

      <p>If you want to unsubscribe, every email has a link at the bottom. If you want your email removed entirely, write me at <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:chris@chrismccann.co">chris@chrismccann.co</a> and I will take care of it.</p>

      <p><strong>Contact</strong></p>

      <p>Questions about any of this: <a class="inline-link" href="mailto:chris@chrismccann.co">chris@chrismccann.co</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
